    "result_text": "The build is green. There's a single test class in the suite and it passes, along with a clean full compile (which regenerates `OwnerDto` from the spec and reruns the MapStruct processor).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was to return a computed `displayName` (formatted `\"LastName, FirstName\"`) when an owner is created and read back. I made two small, well-separated changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` property (readOnly `string`) to the `Owner` schema. Since `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, this gives the DTO its `displayName` field without touching hand-written serialization code.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 populated the field in the single place responsible for `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` translation, via a `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(displayName(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, backed by a small `displayName(Owner)` helper that owns the `\"LastName, FirstName\"` formatting logic.\n\nThe formatting concern lives in the mapper (presentation boundary), not in the `Owner` entity or the create pipeline functions, so the existing OfficeFloor `RespondWithOwnerCreated` step and every other owner response get the field consistently through the same mapper.",
